    "created_at": "2022-05-25T13:45:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-25T13:45:26Z",
    "body": "Sorry, I meant the download-only path does not respect `target`. The fallback-to-normal-navigation-in-a-way-that-goes-against-the-spec path is just a normal navigation, which of course respects `target` and so on, as if we never had the `download` attribute at all: https://browsing-context.glitch.me/download.html.\r\n\r\nBut at least in Chrome, if the download-only path is hit ([conditions are here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_anchor_element.cc;l=439-441;drc=d797bf0d91a1d137996640733d745fdd9eab4bf3)) `target` plays no role.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
